8.12 Midday Analysis
In the first part of the 15-minute cycle, price moved out of a stair-step surge and climbed steadily, refreshing the 64470 phase high; 
After touching the top, bullish momentum quickly dried up, with consecutive large bearish candles that rapidly drove price down to the 63211.6 low, releasing sell-side pressure. After the down move bottomed out, short-term funds entered to repair, producing a rebound characterized by a string of small bullish candles. Currently, price has rebounded into the 63775 range but stalls and closes bearish in the range; rebound momentum has clearly weakened, and in the short term price has returned to a balanced tug-of-war between bulls and bears.

Dual-line structure: DIF turns upward from a low level and crosses above DEA to form a golden cross. Both lines move upward slightly in sync, indicating that short-term bullish momentum has completed a repair. However, the overall values of the dual lines remain in low territory, and bullish momentum strength is relatively weak;

Energy bars: The MACD switches from earlier large bearish green bars to very short, slightly bullish red bars. The red bars are extremely narrow, indicating that after the short-term rebound, bullish momentum lacks follow-through and is unlikely to support sustained upside price movement;

Cycle trend interpretation: Although the dual lines remain above the zero axis, they are very close to it. The broader bearish trend in the medium term has not been reversed. This rebound is only a technical correction following the decline. The continued narrowing of the red bars suggests the short-term rebound is about to end, and there is risk of a second pullback in the future. 

